Z||000000||Phantom Rage||10-23-1999||01:27 PM||||Hey everyone, Yipppeee!!! I found a factory sub box.  I also think I got the factory amp but am not sure, is it located on the side of the center console, passenger side, behind carpet?  I also got the slide swith on the overhead lighting center.  What does that slide do?  Is for volume control, or does it change the tone like a cross over? <BR>Also did I get everything to get that little sucker work? I got all of the harnesses I think. Once again as always thx!!! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||10-23-1999||06:49 PM||||Yep Thats the amp. The slider controls the tone. You need the amp,speaker box, slider switch with the wiring down to the j block and the wiring from the amp to the radio with the tail that goes across and connects to the overhead wires. If you have any problems please let me know. I have done the mod many times. I also know a place to get the speaker for $38 new||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastonpumpgas||10-24-1999||08:54 AM||||Does anyone have a picture of this, I still dont know where it is at???||||reg||5
Z||000003||batboy||10-24-1999||10:18 AM||||Fieros had a premium stereo option that included an amp and subwoofer. The sub mounted in the space up under the passenger side dash. The sub mounted in an enclosure with the sub speaker pointing down toward the floor.<P>I don't believe this was a real common option, but I've seen the sub enclosures for sale a number of times at fairly low prices. This would be a slick way to add a small sub (6 or 6-1/2 inch diameter) without using up much interior space. I heard that someone mounted an 8 inch sub up under the passenger dash in a custom built box.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phantom Rage||10-24-1999||09:48 PM||||Hey thx guys!!!  Hey Tom that sounds great, I might just have to do that.  The speakers cone was deteriated.  There is a local shop that fixes speakers, where I live.  I am going stop on by and see what they think.  Well thx again guys.  Sorry Fastongas no pics, don't know how yet.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000005||spike||10-25-1999||09:25 AM||||1 6 or 8 inch sub is not enough for me. I will stick with my 2 10" subs maybe I will install 2 12", and again with no loss of interior room or seat travel. I like the fact that my system is not hidden and that everyone can see my custom built box. The best part is I have plenty of BASS. If you like hard hitting bass this is the way to go.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88 Fiero||10-25-1999||10:57 AM||||I also..got the sub-woofer for my car..but I am not using the factory sub-woofer. Instead I have a pair of 5 1/2 Bazooka Base Tubes behind the seats and they fit perfectly well.. I am 6'2 and you can really feel and hear the bass...||||reg||1
